# CURSOR AI RULES - CRITICAL PROTECTION RULES
# ⚠️  THESE RULES MUST BE RESPECTED AT ALL TIMES ⚠️
# Position: Root of project - AI must read these rules before any operation

# ============================================================================
# CRITICAL SECURITY RULES - NEVER VIOLATE THESE
# ============================================================================

## 1. ENVIRONMENT FILES - ABSOLUTE PROTECTION
- NEVER delete, overwrite, modify, truncate, or make ANY changes to:
  - `.env` files (any variant: `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.*.local`, `.env.production`, etc.)
  - Any file containing "env" in the name that might contain sensitive credentials
- NEVER access `.env.local` or protected files without EXPLICIT user permission
- NEVER read or display environment variable values in code suggestions
- NEVER hardcode API keys or credentials - always use `process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_*` references
- If environment file changes are needed, ALWAYS ask for explicit permission first

## 2. FILE OPERATIONS - STRICT PROHIBITIONS
- NEVER delete files without explicit user request
- NEVER truncate files (removing content without replacement)
- NEVER break existing functionality when making changes
- NEVER modify core functions without explicit user permission
- NEVER change function signatures, return types, or parameters without permission
- NEVER remove or comment out existing code without explicit request
- ALWAYS preserve existing code structure and patterns

## 3. FUNCTION PROTECTION
- NEVER modify function implementations without explicit user request
- NEVER change function names, parameters, or return types
- NEVER refactor functions unless explicitly asked
- NEVER remove function exports or break function dependencies
- ALWAYS maintain backward compatibility when making changes

## 4. CODE INTEGRITY RULES
- NEVER break existing code that is working
- NEVER introduce breaking changes without explicit permission
- NEVER remove or modify imports that are in use
- NEVER change file paths or directory structures without permission
- ALWAYS test changes before suggesting them
- ALWAYS verify that changes don't break existing functionality

## 5. PROTECTED FILES AND DIRECTORIES
- NEVER modify files in:
  - `.env*` (all variants)
  - `node_modules/`
  - `.git/`
  - `android/` build files
  - `ios/` build files
  - `supabase/migrations/` (database migrations)
  - `package.json` and `package-lock.json` (only with explicit permission)
  - Any file marked as protected in `.cursorignore`

## 6. USER PERMISSION REQUIREMENTS
- ALWAYS ask for explicit permission before:
  - Modifying `.env` files or any environment configuration
  - Deleting any files
  - Changing function signatures or implementations
  - Breaking changes or refactoring
  - Modifying protected files
  - Making changes that could affect app functionality

## 7. CODE SUGGESTION GUIDELINES
- ALWAYS suggest changes rather than implementing them directly for:
  - Environment file modifications
  - Function signature changes
  - Breaking changes
  - File deletions
- ALWAYS explain the impact of changes before implementing
- ALWAYS preserve existing code patterns and conventions
- ALWAYS maintain code consistency with the existing codebase

## 8. ERROR HANDLING
- If asked to modify protected files, politely decline and explain why
- If environment variables are needed, suggest using existing `process.env` references
- If breaking changes are requested, warn the user and ask for confirmation
- Always provide alternatives that don't violate these rules

# ============================================================================
# PROJECT-SPECIFIC RULES
# ============================================================================

## React Native / Expo Project Rules
- Always use `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` prefix for environment variables
- Never modify `app.json`, `eas.json`, or build configuration without permission
- Preserve existing component patterns and structure
- Maintain TypeScript type safety

## API Integration Rules
- Never hardcode API keys - always use environment variables
- Never expose API keys in code, logs, or error messages
- Always use the existing API service patterns

## Database Rules
- Never modify Supabase migrations without explicit permission
- Never change database schema without user approval
- Always preserve existing database structure

# ============================================================================
# REMINDER FOR AI
# ============================================================================
# These rules are positioned at the root of the project for maximum visibility
# Read and respect these rules before EVERY operation
# When in doubt, ask the user for permission
# Better to be cautious than to break something

